incrementally: fetch a finished game once (keyed by \code{game_id}), find new games with one \code{\link[=nl_schedule]{nl_schedule()}} call
per run, and fetch season tables at most once per game day.

Seasons are END years and go on the wire unchanged. Ids (\verb{*_id}) are whole-number \code{numeric} (a 14-digit
\code{game_id} exceeds R's 32-bit integer); every other whole-number column is \code{integer}. The club backend key the
API ships in \verb{/teams/\{id\}/info} is dropped before parsing and never returned.

Endpoint: \verb{GET https://www.nationalleague.ch/api/games/\{gameId\}}.

The six game-page wrappers (\code{\link[=nl_game_overview]{nl_game_overview()}}, \code{\link[=nl_pbp]{nl_pbp()}}, \code{\link[=nl_lineups]{nl_lineups()}}, \code{\link[=nl_player_box]{nl_player_box()}},
